The headwind component is the wind speed times the cosine of the angle between the wind direction and the runway heading. This mirrors the crosswind formula in X10, which uses SIN(DEGREES(U7-X7)). The runway heading is in U7 and the wind direction in X7.

Because the crosswind formula passes the angle through DEGREES(), the same structure is used here with COS.

{"formula": "=X8*COS(DEGREES(U7-X7))"}

