F46 holds x/y = (Easting - L1)/(L4 - Northing), which is tan(Θ). So Θ = ATAN(x/y), which in F47 is =ATAN(F46).

Later formulas such as F67 use COS(F47) directly in radians, which is consistent with F47 being in radians. F48 converts it to degrees with (F47*360)/(2*PI()), which confirms this.

